   "source": [
    "# 05 — Customer Spending Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Builds a regression model to predict the average amount of product spending expected from a customer using demographic, purchase-channel and campaign-related features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.svm import SVC, SVR\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, r2_score, classification_report\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load modelling data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final_df = pd.read_csv(""C:\Users\hp\Downloads\customer_formatted.csv"")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prepare regression target\n",
    "\n",
    "The target is the average of the six product-spending variables used in the original notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = final_df.iloc[: , [0,1,2,3,4,11,12,13,14,15,16,17]].values\n",
    "targets = final_df.iloc[: , [5,6,7,8,9,10]].values\n",
    "Y=[]\n",
    "for row in range(len(targets)):\n",
    "  avg = sum(targets[row])//len(targets[row])\n",
    "  Y.append(avg)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train-test split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_train,x_test,y_train,y_test = train_test_split(X,Y, test_size = 0.2, random_state=0)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train SVR model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "regression_model = SVR(kernel = 'rbf')\n",
    "regression_model.fit(x_train,y_train)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluate using R²"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "preds = regression_model.predict(x_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "score = r2_score(y_test,preds)\n",
    "score = round(score,2)\n",
    "print(f'The model has a R2 score of {score}.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "R² is used in the original analysis to measure how much variability in the target is explained by the regression model."
   ]
  }
